# =====================================================================
# .gitignore — replication package
#
# Principle: the committed tree should EQUAL the distributable package, so that
# `git archive HEAD` (or a GitHub release zip) reproduces it exactly with no
# manual curation. We therefore ignore only:
#   (a) confidential raw source data,
#   (b) generated intermediates,
#   (c) backups and dev/editor/OS artifacts.
# Everything the README lists as "provided" is committed (see notes below).
# =====================================================================

# ── (a) Confidential raw source microdata — never commit ─────────────────────
# Replicators place the confidential INS census / birth / survey files in these
# folders (see README "Data Availability and Provenance"); the read/clean
# scripts also write intermediate CSVs into the year folders. Neither the
# confidential inputs nor those intermediates belong in the repo.
# NOTE: data/raw/other/ (nomenclator code tables) is NOT ignored — it is provided.
data/raw/1992/
data/raw/2002/
data/raw/2011/
data/raw/Birth/
data/raw/survey/
data/raw/shapefiles/
data/raw/elections/

# ── (b) Generated intermediates — reproducible from a run ────────────────────
data/processed/linked/
data/processed/results/

# Provided data that IS committed (listed here for the record; NOT ignored):
#   data/raw/other/             census nomenclators / code tables
#   data/raw census/            SIRUTA + nomenclator code tables
#   data/processed/structural/  structural-model bootstrap results (.rds)
#   data/processed/survey/      anonymized survey extracts + siruta3 lookup

# ── (c) Backups, R / editor artifacts, OS cruft ──────────────────────────────
code/*/bkp/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
*.tmp
*.tmp.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code internal (not part of the replication package)
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
